Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Riemannian Infrageometry", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Riemannian Infrageometry",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " describes and distinguishes graphs as geometric substrates. In contrast, \
synthetic infrageometry asks only whether certain postulates are satisfied by \
the substrate so that its propositions about geometric objects hold. Riemann \
viewed space as an ",
 StyleBox["infinitesimal webbing of paths",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " and, by imposing conditions on the infinitesimal length element, arrived \
at the quadratic metric tensor as the lowest-order data satisfying those \
conditions. This split continuous geometry into a manifold, which carries the \
topology and global analysis, and a Riemannian structure. This led people \
such as Gromov to ask about the moduli space of Riemannian structures on a \
fixed manifold, or, conversely, to derive topological quantities from \
Riemannian ones. In infrageometry, the ",
 StyleBox["discrete webbing of paths",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " given by a graph is itself the geometric substrate, so no such split \
occurs. We relate infrageometry to continuous geometry through rescaled \
Gromov\[Dash]Hausdorff convergence, where the scaling is determined by the ",
 StyleBox["observer's scale",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". This yields a generalized definition of geometry: if a limit of rescaled \
graphs is a metric space arising from a Riemannian manifold, then that \
manifold is uniquely determined up to isomorphism."
}], "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "GuideFunctionsSection",
 CellID->1866139230,ExpressionUUID->"a0ea3657-4c83-4862-93c8-ecf80cebc774"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A geodesic at observer scale ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9c140f62-8e22-4e4e-8a58-e9c2a0cdda41"],
 " of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6dec7160-14d9-4616-9673-4d6bac799e42"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraGeodesic", "[", 
   RowBox[{"germ", ",", " ", "r", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6c40323-78fe-4e19-a228-2622c7108b7c"],
 ", is a family of walks of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "870ef232-e6c6-4a72-ac87-590dd3780cb4"],
 " that are shortest paths in every window of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "efd97c93-297b-4941-b5ae-ada7fe3b77ed"],
 " edges. A representative can be found with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"RandomInfraGeodesic", "[", "...", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50c477a1-b507-4a7a-918c-b8555d13de22"],
 ", and the edge density of the corresponding multi-object with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraMeasurement", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "geodesic", ",", " ", "\"\<EdgeDensity\>\""}], 
   "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8a824876-60cb-4b80-86b0-2522fb3fbdaf"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"97b8d103-2b92-4b3f-b4e5-1f355ee77006"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We can measure the volumes of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraBall", "[", 
   RowBox[{"p", ",", " ", "r0"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a49e5133-ae79-4fec-b403-336c8cb791e1"],
 " for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "0"], "\[LessEqual]", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f4e126bc-43c1-4bc1-96bf-a93985598ea1"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraTube", "[", 
   RowBox[{"axis", ",", " ", "s"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5a29b489-d7ba-4945-a675-2a76d2179ccb"],
 " for any ray or line through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "afc365b3-2646-4020-8b28-9c633d855f9f"],
 " and any thickness ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e21c4673-fe44-458e-81ef-0b6eff68c6c7"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraCone", "[", 
   RowBox[{"axis", ",", " ", "s"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c274468e-8d81-45e7-b574-5fbecc598140"],
 " for slope ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f6b18ca0-862f-477a-82ea-755fa41c0c6c"],
 ". Such measurements have asymptotic expansions in the continuous case and \
can be used to determine limiting curvature components. However, no sphere \
structure exists a priori on ",
 Cell[BoxData["InfraShell"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b6ce3be0-7453-4031-af75-8f8f227b3e40"],
 ", so the limiting linear tensors can be compared only through histograms. \
We can also obtain the histogram of mutual distances between points, which \
constrains the limiting Riemannian manifold."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"57529754-9a82-4c38-a822-20099c8ff1b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraTangentBundle", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43b6193e-4916-43a8-b59f-5a0265c8b492"],
 " which represents vectors at p by rays of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "147ac9b0-b119-46f4-9347-93bf4fb75eb7"],
 ", and these are compactly encoded as chains in the spray graph at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8bbabe6b-e2c7-41ac-8d52-a3abd344cb2e"],
 ". We have an even simpler infra-bundle, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2a6d2ea7-7a81-4bc7-bc4b-716fd0c90bdb"],
 ", that keeps only the endpoints of rays. We have a minimal model of the \
Levi-Civita connection, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection", "[", 
   RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", 
    RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "90daa731-bc17-4f16-8663-b4b42650129d"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraParallelTransport", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"InfraDisplacementBundle", "[", 
     RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}], ",", " ", "walk"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7c69bad-fc02-43eb-b596-50e23f0cd5c4"],
 "."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"317b118b-ad47-4a83-ada4-f8ed9ae400a1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "We also have ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"InfraMetricTensor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "p", ",", " ", "r"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "ba7e9ee1-58c5-4c76-b039-2127160a368a"],
 ", which computes shortest path projections of rays, displacement commutator \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"DisplacementCommutator", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "d1", ",", " ", "d2"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f147cd6-76b4-495e-a0ec-0beca57daca4"],
 ", and addition of displacements via midpoints with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"DisplacementSum", "[", 
   RowBox[{"g", ",", " ", "d1", ",", " ", "d2"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "03f06087-11de-495a-a304-14de64af66e5"],
 ". These can be used to illustrate emergence of linearity."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"c9f790e1-f5e3-4f5e-905f-1ce8cec91ad7"],

Cell["\t", "GuideDelimiter",ExpressionUUID->"89f344c4-494b-4c62-ac39-9b035959b8ae"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Infrageodesics", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"89ffdf5b-5085-4950-be67-f83c245ba3fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraGeodesic"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeodesic", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "b6f976de-7d86-49b4-835c-a3a2368d0dce"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the inert geodesics at infra-scale s through a germ, a vertex list; \
InfraMeasurement reads its graph, the window graph of the forward extensions, \
RandomInfraGeodesic the inextensible simple ones"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"2580516b-0873-4f06-98d8-1cc70f2fc725"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomInfraGeodesic"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/RandomInfraGeodesic", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "edd17cbe-edac-4bdf-918f-97522a25616d"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the geodesics at infra-scale s grown from a germ, a vertex or a walk: every \
window of s consecutive vertices plus the next one is a shortest path; a \
trailing count gives a List of them"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"fe68a227-44f2-46e2-9af0-f13d7bfea5ad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraGeodesicQ"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraGeodesicQ", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "f84c4e64-3d5e-4a22-bc44-37c99d3ac173"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "whether a walk is a geodesic at infra-scale s; scale 1 is InfraWalkQ and \
Infinity is InfraSegmentQ"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"7cc2b616-0d69-4020-a098-033e690133aa"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Shells", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"e308f6b9-4034-4f72-a6ac-96aad4bce2b6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraShell"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraShell", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineGuideFunction",
  TaggingRules->{"PageType" -> "Function"},ExpressionUUID->
  "5e676c76-84b3-4da7-a94a-d1bf83e01898"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the inert shell {v : rmin <= d(c, v) <= rmax} about a vertex or a vertex \
set, a level set of the distance; InfraMeasurement reads its volumes, \
RandomInfraShell its vertices"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"907ffd05-8ca8-42cc-9934-6020212d0343"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraShell"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/FindInfraShell", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
